evidence.en:
function useStore(store) {
  const [value, setValue] = useState(store.get());
  useEffect(() => store.subscribe(() => setValue(store.get())), [store]);
  return value;
}

Symptom: header reads the store early in a long render pass; a price tick
mutates the store mid-render; rows read the new value when rendering resumes.
One committed frame contains two versions of the store — this is called ___b1___.
It became possible because transitions make rendering ___b2___, so a render pass
can span a store write. The fix is replacing the hand-rolled hook with ___b3___,
which re-checks the snapshot and forces a synchronous re-render on conflict.

